flow was $5.7 billion in FY2025: operating cash flow of $8 billion less capital spending of $2.3 billion (computed from two filed figures). That is 20.1% of revenue. In FY2020 it was $3.4 billion.","cites":["AMAT.ocf.2025","AMAT.capex.2025","AMAT.revenue.2025","AMAT.ocf.2020","AMAT.capex.2020"]},{"topic":"sbc","text":"Stock-based compensation was $668 million in FY2025, 2.4% of revenue, against 1.8% in FY2020.","cites":["AMAT.sbc.2025","AMAT.revenue.2025","AMAT.sbc.2020","AMAT.revenue.2020"]},{"topic":"returns","text":"In FY2025 the company paid $4.9 billion to repurchase its own shares and $1.4 billion in dividends: $6.3 billion together (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["AMAT.buybacks.2025","AMAT.dividends.2025"]},{"topic":"quarter","text":"In the three months ended 2026-07-26 revenue was $9.1 billion, up 24.8% from $7.3 billion in the three months ended 2025-07-27.","cites":["AMAT.d.revenue.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","AMAT.d.revenue.2025-04-28.2025-07-27"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Over the four quarters to 2026-07-26 revenue added up to $30.8 billion (computed from five filed figures), operating income to $9.1 billion and net income to $9.3 billion.","cites":["AMAT.d.revenue.2024-10-28.2025-10-26","AMAT.d.revenue.2024-10-28.2025-07-27","AMAT.d.revenue.2025-10-27.2026-01-25","AMAT.d.revenue.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","AMAT.d.revenue.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","AMAT.d.opinc.2024-10-28.2025-10-26","AMAT.d.opinc.2024-10-28.2025-07-27","AMAT.d.opinc.2025-10-27.2026-01-25","AMAT.d.opinc.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","AMAT.d.opinc.2026-04-27.2026-07-26","AMAT.d.netinc.2024-10-28.2025-10-26","AMAT.d.netinc.2024-10-28.2025-07-27","AMAT.d.netinc.2025-10-27.2026-01-25","AMAT.d.netinc.2026-01-26.2026-04-26","AMAT.d.netinc.2026-04-27.2026-07-26"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Free cash flow over the same four quarters was $5.6 billion: operating cash flow of $8.4 billion less capital spending of $2.8 billion (computed from ten filed figures).","cites":["AMAT.d.ocf.2024-10-28.2025-10-26","AMAT.d.ocf.2024-10-28.2025-07-27","AMAT.d.ocf.2025-10-27.2026-01-25","AMAT.d.ocf.2025-10-27.2026-04-26","AMAT.d.ocf.2025-10-27.2026-07-26","AMAT.d.capex.2024-10-28.2025-10-26","AMAT.d.capex.2024-10-28.2025-07-27","AMAT.d.capex.2025-10-27.2026-01-25","AMAT.d.capex.2025-10-27.2026-04-26","AMAT.d.capex.2025-10-27.2026-07-26"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The proxy statement filed 2026-01-28 gives the principal executive officer’s total pay for FY2025 as $29.6 million in its summary compensation table, and the “compensation actually paid” - the SEC’s measure, which revalues share awards over the year - as $87 million.","cites":["AMAT.pay.peoTotal.2025","AMAT.pay.peoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"For the other named executive officers the same table gives an average of $7.6 million in total and $16.3 million actually paid.","cites":["AMAT.pay.neoTotal.2025","AMAT.pay.neoPaid.2025"]},{"topic":"pay","text":"The table puts the value of $100 held in the company’s shares over the years it covers at $392.09 at the end of FY2025, and $313.53 for the peer group the company chose.","cites":["AMAT.pay.tsr.2025","AMAT.pay.peerTsr.2025"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $2.6 billion at the end of FY2025 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiability), against $2.8 billion a year earlier.","cites":["AMAT.deferred.2025","AMAT.deferred.2024"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 36,500 in its own words. FY2025 revenue works out to about $777,000 for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["AMAT.q.employees","AMAT.revenue.2025"]},{"topic":"flags","text":"The FY2025 annual report tags a goodwill impairment of $41 million.","cites":["AMAT.impairment.2025"]},{"topic":"flags","text":"The FY2025 annual report tags restructuring charges of $181 million.","cites":["AMAT.restructuring.2025"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2025 the balance sheet carried $7.2 billion in cash and cash equivalents and $1.3 billion in short-term investments, and $6.6 billion of debt as tagged (LongTermDebtNoncurrent + LongTermDebtCurrent + ShortTermBorrowings). Cash and short-term investments exceeded that debt by $2 billion (computed from five filed figures).","cites":["AMAT.cash.2025","AMAT.sti.2025","AMAT.debtLong.2025","AMAT.debtCurrent.2025","AMAT.debtShort.2025"]}]},"fin":{"AMAT":{"insiders":{"from":"2025-11-23","to":"2026-11-23","complete":true,"listed":52,"read":52,"other":0,"failed":0,"odd":0,"people":[["Sanders Adam","Corp. Controller & CAO"],["BRUNER JUDY","Director"],["Hill Brice","SVP, CFO"],["DICKERSON GARY E","President and CEO, director"],["Raja Prabu G.","President, Semi. Products Grp."],["Nalamasu Omkaram","Senior Vice President, CTO"],["Iannotti Thomas J","Director"],["Deane Timothy M","SVP, Applied Global Services"],["Little Teri A.","SVP, CLO"]],"rows":[["S",0,725,394807.45,"2026-10-02","2026-10-02","0001628280-26-065097","2026-10-05",0],["S",1,1000,465000,"2026-09-08","2026-09-08","0001628280-26-061408","2026-09-10",0],["S",2,7500,3594375.75,"2026-08-25","2026-08-25","0001628280-26-059277","2026-08-27",0],["S",3,78321,55550319.99,"2026-06-29","2026-06-30","0001628280-26-046609","2026-07-01",0],["S",4,10000,6335300,"2026-06-18","2026-06-18","0001628280-26-044741","2026-06-22",0],["S",3,83000,49239083.62,"2026-06-15","2026-06-16","0001628280-26-044046","2026-06-17",0],["S",5,35000,20754197.25,"2026-06-15","2026-06-16","0001628280-26-044048","2026-06-17",0],["S",6,9250,5547872.5,"2026-06-16","2026-06-16","0001628280-26-044050","2026-06-17",0],["S",7,8621,5092984.2,"2026-06-15","2026-06-15","0001628280-26-044039","2026-06-17",0],["S",4,50000,25264196.75,"2026-06-04","2026-06-04","0001628280-26-041314","2026-06-05",0],["S",2,2500,1247153.75,"2026-06-03","2026-06-03","0001628280-26-041310","2026-06-05",0],["S",1,1128,507600,"2026-05-26","2026-05-26","0001628280-26-038923","2026-05-28",0],["S",0,268,116369.89,"2026-05-22","2026-05-22","0001628280-26-038261","2026-05-26"